License boundaries in this repository
=====================================

This repository is MIT-licensed overall (see LICENSE), except:

* patches/kernel/*.patch are Linux kernel patches, licensed GPL-2.0-only.
  Each patch file's header records its provenance; those headers are
  preserved verbatim.
* dts/liuqin-abl-boot-overlay.dts is GPL-2.0-only (device-tree source,
  carried unchanged from the downstream project).
* pkgs/liuqin-power-keyd/liuqin-power-keyd.c, liuqin-power-key-action.sh
  and liuqin-power-menu.py are MIT, carried from the downstream project
  (yzddmr6/xiaomipad-6pro-mainline).
* data/ucm2/ (ALSA UCM2 configuration) is BSD-3-Clause per upstream
  alsa-ucm-conf; the liuqin card files originate from the downstream
  project.
* data/sensors-patches/*.patch are patches to hexagonrpc (GPL-2.0) and
  iio-sensor-proxy (GPL-3.0 / LGPL); they retain their downstream headers.
* pkgs/firmware.nix and pkgs/sensors-config.nix reference proprietary
  Qualcomm/Xiaomi binaries that are NOT redistributable. This repository is
  PRIVATE / personal self-use and must not be published publicly: the
  committed data/*.tar.zst archives (liuqin-firmware-*, stock-dtbo-entries,
  stock-base-dtbs) are the operator's own device / stock ROM dumps. The SSC
  sensor archive is an uncommitted `requireFile` input supplied by the
  operator. If the
  repository is ever to be published, these files must first be removed
  from history (git filter-repo --path-glob 'data/*.tar.zst'
  --invert-paths) and data/stock-dtbo-entries.nix / stock-base-dtbs.nix
  switched back to requireFile inputs.

Vendor-derived data in the device patches
-----------------------------------------

The camera patches embed register tables decoded from Xiaomi/Qualcomm binaries
and fall under the same PRIVATE / personal-self-use caveat as the firmware
above; none of the source containers is committed.

* patches/kernel/0019 (IMX596, SC202CS) and 0020 (S5KJN1 vendor modes) carry
  sensor init/mode tables extracted from the MIUI sensor-module containers
  (com.qti.sensormodule.*.bin); they were machine-generated during bring-up
  (the generator lived in the bring-up branch).
* patches/kernel/0018 carries the CSIPHY 2.1.3 lane table extracted from the
  vendor camera.ko during bring-up.

If the repository is ever published, treat these tables with the same care as
data/*.tar.zst (see the filter-repo note above).

Knowledge (partition geometry, ABL behavior, systemd ordering rationale)
was extracted from the downstream project and re-expressed in Nix; no
downstream shell scripts are used in the build chain.
